## AI-Assisted

## Print the derivative-maker container image reference, and nothing else.
##
## ONE definition, because three places consume it -- docker-run (builds and runs
## it), ci/dm-docker-image-cache (saves and loads it) and the CI workflows (start
## a systemd container from it). A copy that drifts does not fail loudly: docker
## simply pulls or builds a DIFFERENT image, so a stale copy silently runs the
## wrong container.
##
## The tag is arch-qualified so an amd64 and an arm64 image can never collide in
## a shared docker store or image cache. The image is built natively, so its
## architecture is the host's; 'uname --machine' (e.g. x86_64 / aarch64) names it
## unambiguously.

set -o errexit
set -o nounset
set -o pipefail
set -o errtrace
shopt -s inherit_errexit
shopt -s shift_verbose

printf '%s\n' "kicksecure/derivative-maker-docker:$(uname --machine)"
